A static web page that runs CipherLoop-S, a 241,758-parameter substitution-cipher
solver, entirely in the browser. Model and training code:
https://github.com/wumich15/cipherloop

CipherLoop builds on ALICE (https://github.com/al-jshen/alice), Copyright (c)
Jeff Shen and Lindsay M. Smith, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(see third_party/ALICE_LICENSE.txt). cipherloop.js is a JavaScript port of
model code adapted from ALICE; its header describes the changes. J. Shen and
L. M. Smith, "ALICE: An
Interpretable Neural Architecture for Generalization in Substitution Ciphers",
arXiv:2509.07282.

Model weights (model/weights.bin) were trained on QUOTES500K -- S. Goel,
R. Madhok, S. Garg, "Proposing Contextually Relevant Quotes for Images",
ECIR 2018 (doi:10.1007/978-3-319-76941-7_49); original release
https://github.com/ShivaliGoel/Quotes-500K, made publicly available by its
authors "for educational and research purposes". This site is non-commercial.
No dataset text is included here.

The page's visual style is modeled on Autograder.io's open-source frontend
(https://github.com/eecs-autograder/ag-website-vue, LGPL-3.0). No code from it
is included; this site is not affiliated with Autograder.io or the University
of Michigan.
